<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  A partial Info.plist, merged into the one `GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES`
	  builds. Everything else this app declares is still a build setting; this
	  file exists for the one key Xcode's generator does not know.

	  `INFOPLIST_KEY_UIBackgroundModes = audio` is accepted as a build setting,
	  survives `-showBuildSettings`, and never reaches the built Info.plist —
	  the generator has a fixed list of keys it understands and this is not one
	  of them. It failed completely silently, and what it would have cost is the
	  whole feature: without the audio background mode iOS suspends this app the
	  moment the user switches to the app they are writing in, which is the only
	  moment dictation is ever used. `Scripts/prove-dictation.sh` check 2 reads
	  the built plist, not the build setting, for exactly that reason.

	  The recording session is also the *only* thing this mode is for. Nothing
	  here plays audio, and a session closes itself after 5, 15 or 60 minutes —
	  see `SharedStore.dictationSessionMinutes`, which deliberately has no
	  "never".
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
